//RS //! Post-sema compiler-extension hook (D-DX5-HOOK1=A / Tower #549).
//RS //!
//RS //! When `JET_COMPILER_EXTENSION` names a `compiler-extension-v1` `.wasm`,
//RS //! the driver freezes a typed read-only snapshot after sema and sends it to
//RS //! the sibling `jetpack` compiler-extension host. Wasmtime never links into
//RS //! the compiler process. No new user syntax — env registration only until a
//RS //! spelling ballot. Failures are Jet-owned (E1402); guests never crash the
//RS //! compiler or expose rustc (I2/I3).
//RS //!
//RS //! Tower #549 C5 proofs live in `tests` below (host/SDK/diagnostic + AOT/dev
//RS //! fact parity). Repository-wide verification runs at multi-card milestones.
//RS 
